Z||000000||jlruiz67||08-23-2000||09:29 PM||||Hello all<BR>Just came back from the mufler shop. They installed a 80 series street muffler part number 42583 it cost a total of $200. Now I don't know if that's a good deal for you but for me it was a great deal. In case you live near Orange County California the shop is <P>Plaza Mufflers <BR>Chris<BR>237 West Chapman Avenue  714-639-6460.<P>||||reg||14
Z||000001||crazygt||08-23-2000||09:39 PM||||Hi there <BR>How does the flowmaster sound install on your fiero.I was thinking of geting one as well but wasn't sure how loud it was going to be.  <p>[This message has been edited by crazygt (edited 08-23-2000).]||||reg||7
Z||000002||jlruiz67||08-23-2000||09:56 PM||||I installed the new muffler because my original had a big hole in it and sounded horrible, so it is really hard for me to tell how loud it really is because its not as loud as the old one. It does sound deep and when I punch the gas you can hear the power. Sorry I wasn't much help but at least I now know that the 80 series flowmaster worked for me without modifications, the support brackets are welded to the exaust pipes right out of the muffler they did a great job.||||reg||14
Z||000003||Zorba||08-24-2000||01:48 AM||||42583 Single 2.50" Inlet/ Dual 2.50" Outlet, 4"x9.75"x15" $72.95 <P>Is this the one that you installed? Do you have v-4 or v-6 car? I wonder which one would go well with a  4 cylinder if yours is a v6?<BR> ||||reg||5
Z||000004||jlruiz67||08-24-2000||02:13 AM||||Zorba:<BR>I have the V6 and you are correct on the model, size and mail order price of $72||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||08-24-2000||08:17 AM||||I had a 40 series on my SE that GT Bastard has now and i't NOT loud inside the car.. but out side the car it has a VERY powerful sound and deffinatly turns heads! I loved it... ||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||08-24-2000||12:02 PM||||In this case the single/dual outlet issue is mostly dependant on what tail is on the car. Some 4's have dual outlets but most are singles. The tail pipes are so short that performance wise it's not going to make any diferance if it's single or dual.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Blade||08-24-2000||12:55 PM||||Jlruiz...are you in a car club out here?<BR>Im looking into joining one as soon as i get my car...Im in Orange County as well. Fullerton. <P>Blade||||reg||1
Z||000008||dman||08-24-2000||03:10 PM||||Hello everyone. This is a little off topic but I thought some of you Orange County guys might want to know about Fieros West. In case you don't know about them they are located in Southern California. I think they (in conjunction with a San Diego club and AZ fiero club) helped coordinate the recent WestFest in San Diego.<P>They have a webpage (which hasn't been updated in a while) located here:<BR> <A HREF="http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/" TARGET=_blank>http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/</A> <P>I haven't signed up as a member yet since I have so little time but I have had a chance to meet some of the members and they seem like a really great bunch of people.<P>And jlruiz67, glad to hear about your flowmaster and thanks for sharing the info about that muffler shop.<p>[This message has been edited by dman (edited 08-24-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Zorba||08-24-2000||06:24 PM||||I just unhooked the muffler on my 4 banger and run a straight pipe to dual resonating tips. So all i have now is the cat and the tips. The sound is throatier but nothing to turn heads unless they think I have a hole in my exhaust pipe! ( <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Sounds throatier though. The v8's and v6 do better at the sound part when it comes to exhaust modifications. ||||reg||6
Z||000010||Blade||08-24-2000||06:56 PM||||Dman thats the club i am planning on joining. :P<P>Blade||||reg||1
Z||000011||rockcrawl||08-24-2000||08:35 PM||||I've got the flowmaster 42583 Single 2.50" Inlet/ Dual 2.50" Outlet on my 3.8 car and it sounds awesome! I can't see how it fit without modification though, it is huge compared to the stock muffler, not to mention the much larger pipe diameter. Don't plan on buying that muffler and just bolting it on. I think Chris West makes a modified flowmaster that fits much better. The Flowmaster website <A HREF="http://www.flomastermuffler.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.flomastermuffler.com</A>  has details of all their mufflers, and none of them are a direct fit for the Fiero with dual outlets. <P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||1
Z||000012||AL||08-24-2000||09:16 PM||||hey ruiz i didn't know you where close, maybe we should get together and compare flowmasters,now  don't want to start another war of words on this subject since mine got out of hand but if you need a pic of the flowmaster that we are talkin about i can supply it.once you hear this flowmaster in your car you won't regret buying it.<B>AL</B>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/AL_sig.gif">   <P>------------------<BR> <P><p>[This message has been edited by AL (edited 08-24-2000).]||||reg||14
