Z||000018||jlruiz67||08-25-2000||01:07 AM||||"I can't see how it fit without modification though, it is huge compared to the stock muffler, not to mention the much larger pipe diameter."<P>I had to convince the muffler shop that it would work and that I had seen it in a Fiero before (the only knowlage of it working was Al's post from a few months back and his emails that included the sound an more pics) It took 20 minutes of talk to get the job started and then 1hr later the job was done with no modifications to the muffler. They cut the in and outlet pipes as recomended by flowmaster in its installation instructions, they then trimed the existing pipes after removing the old muffler (outside the car)and tack welded the muffer in place and then they put it up to test fitting, It was perfect. After they welded the hole thing they installed 2 muffler hangers on the 2 outlet pipes and that was it. No modifications done to the 80 series p/n 42583. All I have to say is that this muffler works without modifications in a tight fit. ||||reg||1
